Which of the following programs correctly reverses a string?
Option A:
String s = "hello";
for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {
System.out.print(s.charAt(i));
}
Option B:
String s = "hello";
if (s.length() > 0) {
System.out.println(s);
}
Option C:
String s = "hello";
for (int i = 0; i <= s.length(); i++) {
System.out.print(s.charAt(i));
}
Option D:
String s = "hello";
String rev = "";
for (int i = s.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
rev += s.charAt(i);
}
System.out.println(rev);

